{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1366065-raiding-a-shipment-of-tribute","id":1366065,"title":"Raiding a shipment of Tribute","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-07T10:53:36-08:00","id":1366065,"title":"Raiding a shipment of Tribute","content":"So.... the Little Band of Celestial Exalts (one Lunar and two Solars) have decided to liberate some Tribute on its way to the Realm.<br /> <br /> We're playing in Zhaojun, based in Goldenseal, and it's been established that tribute is sent twice per year and that V'neef is tasked with transporting it via their Merchant Fleet.<br /> <br /> One of the characters has some bad history with the Satrap (who is a V'neef) from before exalting, and all three want to liberate Zhaojun from the Realm, and will therefore be waiting until after the Tribute has been transferred and transported for a while with the Merchant Fleet - maximizing the damage to the V'neef.<br /> <br /> I am looking for some advice to not completely go off the charts here:<br /> <br /> 1. I assume that the level of wealth given in a half-year tribute from Zhaojun is pretty massive. I am thinking somewhere between 10-20 times the Resource 5 level of Jade/Silver + other stuff.<br /> 2. Transport will probably happen in a couple of serious merchant ships with escort ships.<br /> <br /> What I'm not sure about is how much security it is likely that they muster for this type of travel? And is the level of Tribute way off?<br /> <br /> Any advice would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1474-rouharu","name":"Rouharu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T11:42:32-08:00","id":1366079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rouharu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1366065-raiding-a-shipment-of-tribute#post1366065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am looking for some advice to not completely go off the charts here:<br /> <br /> 1. I assume that the level of wealth given in a half-year tribute from Zhaojun is pretty massive. I am thinking somewhere between 10-20 times the Resource 5 level of Jade/Silver + other stuff.<br /> 2. Transport will probably happen in a couple of serious merchant ships with escort ships.<br /> <br /> What I'm not sure about is how much security it is likely that they muster for this type of travel? And is the level of Tribute way off?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Resources system is, of course, deliberately abstracted, so it's a bit tricky to pin down &quot;how much&quot; this would be in those terms. For one thing, when you say &quot;10-20 times the Resource 5 level&quot;, do you mean &quot;enough money to make 10-20 Resources 5 purchases&quot;? Or more &quot;enough money to give 10-20 people Resources 5 fortunes <i>permanently</i>&quot;? The former is easily within what I'd see as a reasonable tribute level. The latter is not impossible, and I'd expect more from particularly rich satrapies (Harborhead is probably putting out more than that, specifically in the form of jade, for example). To determine if it's reasonable, I'd suggest estimating a) how big Zhaojin is, and b) what percentage of people do you think could reasonably achieve the highest level of economic prosperity possible for an individual every year. If the latter number is smaller than your figure of 10-20 Resource 5 fortunes, then the satrapy is being reduced, economically, by the Realm's tribute. Whereas if it's higher, the satrapy is not being <i>completely</i> reduced, and there are surplus resources about. Personally, I think that the Realm under the Empress probably aimed to have most satrapies pretty much right at the zero-growth level - extracting enough money so that there was no significant surplus, but not actively shrinking, either. That way, satrapies would mostly continue to be productive, but couldn't grow their own economy or political power to potentially challenge the Realm, and there was the potential stick of &quot;we could extract <i>more</i> tribute from you&quot; hanging over them. Whereas these days, post-Empress, I'm thinking most satrapies are being looted, to a greater or lesser degree, by the Great House that controls them.<br /> <br /> For security, given that level of resources, I'd probably suggest essentially a small army. There would be multiple ships, for one thing - you wouldn't want to risk losing all that tribute with the sinking of one vessel, if nothing else. I'd probably call it at least one ship per Resource 5 purchase, personally, and maybe 4-5 ships per Resource 5 fortune. So you're looking at a fleet somewhere between 10 and 100 ships, depending on how much tribute is being sent. Each ship should have a contingent of troops. I'd probably put that at Magnitude 2 for typical ships, and use the Battle-Ready Troops stats. Besides those, there would be a collection of better troops assigned to the fleet in general, and moved about as whoever was in charge of security thought necessary. I'd put a Magnitude 2 unit of elite troops for every 10 ships, roughly. And there should definitely be Dragon-Blooded around to help with this as well. I'd peg that as one Essence 2 DB for every 10 ships, and a higher Essence DB for every 4-5 &quot;regular&quot; DBs, serving as a commander. And no matter how big the fleet is, there should be at least one DB with the highest Essence who's the admiral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T12:26:38-08:00","id":1366089,"title":"","content":"I think normally tribute is a monthly deal for wealthy satrapies but might go down to twice yearly if they\u2019re just not producing that much. Or if they worked out a deal to send it in two huge bulk shipments.<br /> <br /> If you have The Realm book there\u2019s some awesome stats and suggestions for imperial treasure fleets on page 80-82. I don\u2019t just want to repost it here, but some bits that might inform you are that the treasure fleet has roughly 1,000 ships, making it the second smallest Realm fleet, and its captains are trained in anti-piracy tactics. If the shipments are massive and important enough they may even deploy First Age vessels in their protection.<br /> <br /> Either way I\u2019d definitely pick up The Realm if you have the spare funds, it\u2019s full of good content for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T13:03:33-08:00","id":1366098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1366065-raiding-a-shipment-of-tribute?p=1366079#post1366079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd put a Magnitude 2 unit of elite troops for every 10 ships, roughly. And there should definitely be Dragon-Blooded around to help with this as well. I'd peg that as one Essence 2 DB for every 10 ships, and a higher Essence DB for every 4-5 &amp;quot;regular&amp;quot; DBs, serving as a commander. And no matter how big the fleet is, there should be at least one DB with the highest Essence who's the admiral.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! This sounds reasonable I guess. Zhaojun, detailed in the Realm is supposed to be a really right country - the most prosperous in the South-West.<br /> <br /> So based on your comments I am thinking I should probably go into the high-end or above of my estimate for the total haul.<br /> <br /> Sorry for being unclear on the Resource meaning, I figure I would use the estimated yearly income for Resource 5 as the \u201cunit\u201d, and that the half-year tribute would be some multiplication of that.<br /> <br /> Good point about the size of the fleet. I was probably underselling it a bit. Will add ships.<br /> <br /> I have no idea how this will play out in a straight up confrontation. \ud83d\ude05<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1366065-raiding-a-shipment-of-tribute?p=1366089#post1366089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think normally tribute is a monthly deal for wealthy satrapies but might go down to twice yearly if they\u2019re just not producing that much. Or if they worked out a deal to send it in two huge bulk shipments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I guess I went more for the Story on this one. Bigger event when it's half-yearly, and a more serious hit to the Satrap if it goes broken.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the pointer on the Realm! I haven't read that book thoroughly enough. But I love what I've read, and the section you pointed out is great for this purpose!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1474-rouharu","name":"Rouharu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T13:09:13-08:00","id":1366099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rouharu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1366065-raiding-a-shipment-of-tribute?p=1366098#post1366098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good point about the size of the fleet. I was probably underselling it a bit. Will add ships.<br /> <br /> I have no idea how this will play out in a straight up confrontation. \ud83d\ude05</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that, while the whole fleet might be that size, it won't necessarily all travel in one big group. There's safety in numbers, certainly, but that also raises their odds of all being taken out at once by a natural disaster or some kind of supernatural attack that can cover a big area. The admiral in charge might break the fleet down into smaller groups travelling a day or so apart in order to avoid that kind of thing. That gives the tactical specialists in the Circle something to do, trying to estimate which group is the best to hit, and how to avoid them bringing in reinforcements. I'd just say that each group should probably have at least one Dragon-Blood, if not more, in it, to ensure that there's a significant combat encounter no matter which group the PCs hit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T13:38:46-08:00","id":1366102,"title":"","content":"Oh, absolutely. It won\u2019t be 1k ships. But my \u201ctwo merchant ships and some escort ships\u201d is probably a bit small.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1474-rouharu","name":"Rouharu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T14:15:09-08:00","id":1366111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1366065-raiding-a-shipment-of-tribute?p=1366089#post1366089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIf you have The Realm book there\u2019s some awesome stats and suggestions for imperial treasure fleets on page 80-82.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's additional discussion of tribute on pages 149-150. (It specifies that tribute is typically sent once or twice a year, though of course you can change that for your game if you prefer.)<br /> <br /> Also, Zhaoj\u016bn is a favorite of mine, so I'm always happy to hear that it's getting more love in someone's campaign!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T17:41:04-08:00","id":1366179,"title":"","content":"I dunno if I'd use <i>elite</i> troop stats for the crew of the Realm ships; those are the sorts of people who have a sword placed in their hand as soon as they're young enough to make a fist. Probably just use regular battle-ready soldiers or pirates, and one or two elites separate from the mass unit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T17:48:25-08:00","id":1366183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1366065-raiding-a-shipment-of-tribute?p=1366179#post1366179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno if I'd use <i>elite</i> troop stats for the crew of the Realm ships; those are the sorts of people who have a sword placed in their hand as soon as they're young enough to make a fist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that when I mentioned elite troops (and, indeed, <i>all</i> the troops I mentioned) were in addition to the crew of the ships. I agree that the crew of most of them, at least, would probably be lower level. But I think that the ships would also be carrying troops for security, and those, at least some of them, would be higher-quality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}